# Independent review of graph/3.1.kg (the NUMS.Go core package). One review node per claim, each naming the digest it read.

n: 9.5.1
kind: hub
name: review-of-nums-core
is: All 39 claims of 3.1.kg (22 observations, 17 findings) were read against their sources: 32 confirmed, 7 amended (3.1.1.1, 3.1.1.6, 3.1.2.3, 3.1.3.5, 3.1.3.6, 3.1.8.5, 3.1.9.4), none disputed, none left unreviewed; the file has no relayed web claim. Every cited NUMS.Go line was opened, the build was run as checked in and in a fresh copy with the four lines removed, and the dump, the 17 probes and the three shipped samples were run again from that copy.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 9.5.1.1
kind: review
re: 3.1.1.1
saw: 5e063675
ack: node
is: Commits, dates, ec1f742 and the subject of b508f08 are as stated (git log). Two clauses do not hold: the http tree does import nums, and not all later work is under http/. The node should say: later work is under http/ (15,292 lines of Go) apart from two edits of test/sample.go, and http/ still imports nums in one leftover file.
why: NUMS.Go/http/playground.go:14 imports [org]/nums and line 61 calls nums.NewFileParserFromFileName inside a function nothing calls (file last changed 2023-02-13); NUMS.Go/http/go.mod lines 5 and 13 replace and require the module. The 14 commits after ec1f742 all touch http/, and two of them (3111bb4 of 2023-04-02, 9e6bbb4 of 2023-04-05) also change test/sample.go.
by: r3/review-nums-core
