n: 9.5.1.6
kind: review
re: 3.1.1.6
saw: fa81f991
ack: node
is: Every construct was run again from the study's 17 probe files and behaves as stated, except that the study's probes do not show logic: no probe file and neither example file contains &&, || or !. A reviewer probe (if !a && b || a, with n += 2 and n++) is recorded and prints back unchanged, so 'logic' is true of nums but rests on that probe, not on the study's.
why: Two details the statement flattens: range is recorded as 'Access range' over auto-declared globals with the loop body under it, not as a Loop node; go and defer on a later-declared callee are recorded with the no-node ID 0.0.0.0 in the callee position.
