n: 9.5.1.11
kind: review
re: 3.1.2.3
saw: bed53d34
ack: node
is: The 18 and 19 types, the four non-Go instances and the comments are at the cited lines. The last sentence is not what the code does: in an assignment statement the category is TempWrite only when the left side is itself an Access node (dereference, member, subscript) that holds no global and no member, and Write otherwise (go.go:627-630, emit_recipe.go:84-86, 399-413); only the write lowered from ':=' applies the stated rule (go.go:655, emit_recipe.go:392-397).
why: Run in a fresh copy: 's := 0' gives 2.5.5 TempWrite; 's = 1', 's += n' and 'n = 2' on a local or a parameter give 2.6.5 or 2.6.6 Write; '*p = 3' through a pointer parameter gives 2.5.5 TempWrite; 't.x = 4' and 'G = 5' give 2.6.5 Write.
by: r3/review-nums-core
at: 2026-11-24

