ack: node
is: Thirteen languages, Go-only dispatch and the not-supported error are as stated. RegisterGo makes 75 dispatch entries (go.go:1427-1501) that name 68 distinct functions, keyed by 75 of the 213 symbol constants. A comment stands directly above 62 of the 65 handlers of go.go, not each: true_literal, false_literal and nil_literal (go.go:1197-1207) have none.
why: The 68 are the 65 handlers of go.go and the generic Token, Sequence and Choice of parser.go:631-657, which carry no rule comment (Sequence is registered five times, Token three, int_literal twice). All 213 constants, not only twelve, equal the enum in golang/parser.c of the pinned module in the local cache (compared name by name, no difference).
by: r3/review-nums-core
