n: 9.5.1.31
kind: review
re: 3.1.8.5
saw: baa16e8b
ack: node
is: The catalogue is drawn from several languages, and its comment declares the intent of the split: TempWrite is a write with 'no global state change' (nums_consts.go:133-134). The Go handlers do not keep it: a plain assignment to a local or a parameter is recorded as Write, and a write through a pointer parameter as TempWrite (go.go:627-630, emit_recipe.go:84-86; the run is in review 9.5.1.11). The finding should say that the catalogue names an effect split which the implementation does not carry, so effect in the category is an intent to carry forward, not a demonstrated property.
by: r3/review-nums-core
at: 2026-11-24

