n: 9.5.1.37
kind: review
re: 3.1.9.4
saw: b0c09e62
ack: node
is: The premise 3.1.3.6 and emit_recipe.go:232-304 give four outcomes, not one: an unresolved name becomes a local in a variable declaration, a function when it is called, a member when it follows a package or a struct, and a global otherwise. 'Turns every misspelled name into a new global' should read 'turns a misspelled name into a new local, function, member or global, according to where it stands'. Reading a file without its imports is shown by the import probe: fmt.Println is recorded through an empty package.
